SY_TALK("HEdiAA_F0JM",[[0,["Really?"]],[1,["I can't...can't focus."]],[3,["The whole mind is conditioned."]],[5,["I mean, absolutely. It is like a record.","Like a gramophone record going round."]],[8,["Yes. I have seen this in China when,","I went there when Mao was there."]],[14,["See, the girl used to tell us","anything as if it was a record."]],[18,["She was just saying it, without even thinking about it."]],[23,["See then I felt that this is some sort","of a possession this girl has got."]],[27,["But now, of course, Chinese have got their","freedom and they are much better people,"]],[30,["I mean they’re not that kind."]],[32,["But in the beginning, they did that like that in","China and this is how they just conditioned them."]],[41,["But all our theological colleges,","all these people are the same."]],[45,["They are just trying to find","out how to condition people."]],[52,["I mean, if they give all their business and just","take to God, they will be so very much happier."]],[58,["And all this effort will be lost."]],[63,["Very serious things. You see, for","Christian community especially I think,"]],[69,["it is that because of these","barriers, they may never reach God."]],[76,["It’s all right for Christians in the West because","they have seen the nonsense of it, most of them."]],[82,["But in the countries like ours,","you see which are developing,"]],[87,["for them Christianity being","so sophisticated, so good,"]],[91,["you see to them, Christians mean something great."]],[97,["My husband was telling Me that his own uncle wanted to become a Christian because he found that Hindu religion was so absurd,"]],[107,["and the priests were so absurd."]],[109,["So he was so enamoured by Christians."]],[114,["I tell you."]],[121,["I suppose our biggest","problem is the Christians."]],[123,["We really don’t have any other barrier here."]],[128,["We have quite a few Muslims.","They can be a bit fanatical too."]],[134,["And the conversion, you see.","Conversion is another problem."]],[138,["Conversion in India is more in the places","where there are jungles and things"]],[147,["where the people are","absolutely away from society."]],[149,["So for them, money is very important,"]],[152,["and the way these people take the missionaries and their","food and this and that, so they are converting you."]],[159,["I mean donkeys after donkeys."]],[161,["But they have created","problems for us in the way,"]],[164,["that these people say who are living in Khasia, Jaintia, all","these places you see – a former Nagaland sort of a thing."]],[176,["And this Nagaland business","is all a Christian problem."]],[180,["They have all become Christians you","see and don’t understand anything."]],[184,["At the time of Christ, I don’t","know if He ever went to this;"]],[190,["it’s such primitive people."]],[192,["But Christianity has gone to them. They","don’t understand anything – A to Z."]],[197,["Now they came to Lal Bahadur","Shastri, our Prime Minister"]],[202,["and they said that, “We","must have our sovereignty.”"]],[206,["That’s what they said. They had written","it down in their language, ‘sovereignty’."]],[210,["So Shastriji asked, “What is sovereignty?”"]],[212,["“That we don’t know. We","want our sovereignty.”"]],[217,["“Then, what is sovereignty you want?”"]],[220,["Then they said, “This is what","we have. We know one thing.”"]],[224,["Then they said, “But what is it? That we","don’t know.”  “But why do you want it?”"]],[230,["“That we don’t know.  We","want our sovereignty.”"]],[235,["To the Prime Minister! The Prime Minister","said, “Oh God, these Christians.”"]],[239,["And they were wearing suits and hats, funny hats","and suits and all Western dresses, you see."]],[246,["And they are all Christians in","Nagaland. And all stupid people."]],[251,["This is what they had got it, you see on a","paper. “We want our sovereignty.”  Finished."]],[258,["He could have given them anything."]],[262,["I was thinking, he should have given them some sort of an","odd paper and said, “This is sovereignty, you take it back.”"]],[269,["They would have taken it."]],[272,["Such things they have got. And it’s created a","problem; this Nagaland is a problem for India now."]],[279,["It’s the missionaries who have created."]],[281,["Yes, the missionaries."]],[282,["(in Marathi) They wrote it down in their language, “You","go and meet Shastriji and when you go there tell him,"]],[287,["we want our sovereignty, finished.”"]],[290,["But Shastriji was non-plussed. He said,"]],[292,["(in Marathi) “Then what next?”"]],[295,["And in English, you see,","\"We want our sovereignty.”"]],[299,["(in Marathi) “Why do you want","it, sir?” “That we do not know."]],[302,["We want our sovereignty.”"]],[306,["I tell you. When Shashtriji told","us, I didn’t know where to look."]],[310,["He said, “But this is too much. Just written","down that word in English, I mean this sentence"]],[315,["and they were reading it out to me all the time. They would","not say what is sovereignty, why sovereignty – nothing.”"]],[320,["Now missionaries, these then educated."]],[323,["Now the idea of missionaries – because","Church is always confused with..."]],[329,["I mean the ruling people, like the kings and queens and also politics –"]],[336,["so now they are confused with that."]],[338,["So they want to create","a Christian land there."]],[342,["As it is, we have one Hindu","land, one Muslim land."]],[346,["Then we have one Sikh land. Then we’ll have one","Christian land. And there’s one Bangla land."]],[351,["So I don’t know how many parts of that country there","are going to be, of according to the religion."]],[356,["And nobody follows it, that’s the best part of it."]],[362,["And if you see, I saw the other day when","our Prime Minister went to Nagaland,"]],[366,["they made him wear a hat","and he was dancing there."]],[370,["You wear a hat according to them it's Christian."]],[372,["You see, many Christians in India","believe that Christ was born in England."]],[380,["And that he was himself a Christian."]],[382,["He himself...  er?"]],[383,["that he was a Christian."]],[385,["Yes. He Himself was a Christian","and was born in England."]],[388,["This they believe, actually","they believe in it."]],[391,["See there is a story, an interesting story of a villager who","was living… he used to come to Allahabad from his village."]],[399,["And he became a Christian."]],[401,["So he would always go to the river","Ganges, have a bath and go back."]],[405,["So the priest told them, “Now you can’t do, you","see, your religion has changed, you cannot do that."]],[412,["Now you have become a Christian.","You can’t go to the river.”"]],[414,["River Ganges, the Christians","don’t go in India, do you know?"]],[419,["They don’t go to the river Ganges."]],[421,["So, he said in his own language, “Sir, I have become","a ‘sahib’,” means, I have become an Englishman."]],[428,["“But I cannot give up my religion.”"]],[431,["He thought he had become a sahib."]],[445,["And the names are also, they will","change it like this you see. Like a......"]],[450,["like this gentleman’s name was Blondie. So ‘bhura’ (blond) means ‘bhura’."]],[455,["So he said, “Give me a good","name, like Alexander’s name.”"]],[458,["So they called him","Alexander Bhura, you see."]],[462,["So his name was Alexander Bhura, so he thought","he had become a sahib you see, an Englishman."]],[468,["“And now they are asking me to give up my religion also, is","too much. I can’t give up my religion. I will go to Gangaji.”"]],[478,["It’s very sad though, what","the missionaries did."]],[481,["I know in Hawaii and places like that, they destroyed what, from what I’ve read, appears to have been a very enlightened religion,"]],[495,["which would have allowed, for","instance, Sahaja Yoga to just…"]],[500,["they would have understood it instantly."]],[502,["And the Christians just chopped it off."]],[505,["In one generation. Of course the things that Cortez","did in Central America; terrible. Every....."]],[513,["Horrible things…"]],[514,["Every book that had ever been… held any","knowledge that the Aztec came was destroyed."]],[521,["I mean, there is a history","behind the whole thing"]],[524,["Thank God Columbus missed","his point, went to America."]],[528,["Otherwise, there would have","been no Sahaja Yoga here."]],[533,["There would be all Americans","roaming around in India, I think."]],[538,["With their AIDS, or with that kind of a trouble that","they have, because that would have been the thing."]],[556,["I think Hanumana must have done","that job, to take Columbus away."]],[561,["Because I can’t understand. This fellow, such","a clever man, went all the way from England."]],[570,["I mean from… Columbus was from Portuguese, was he?"]],[575,["From Portugal, he went to a place –","Spanish, he was Spanish, I think: Spanish."]],[581,["He should have gone to India, I don’t","know how he reached America, you see."]],[586,["So must be Hanumana’s trick."]],[591,["That’s a long way."]],[593,["That’s what, he was there. But","they killed all the people."]],[597,["He did call that continent India."]],[600,["Yes they killed...."]],[601,["That’s why we have the Red Indians."]],[602,["Yes. Red Indians. But the poor Red Indians","were killed and massacred completely."]],[607,["I mean the white people wherever they","went, they massacred all kinds."]],[611,["You see, the French, the","Portuguese… I tell you,"]],[614,["the Portuguese now they look so horrid."]],[617,["But when they came to India – near Bombay,","you must have seen that Trimurti and all that."]],[624,["Did you go to see that Trimurti?"]],[626,["That’s such a rock, black rock."]],[630,["And to hewn into it with this beauty","was really… must have been remarkable."]],[635,["But these people thought this rock","cannot be broken with anything,"]],[638,["so they took cannons on","the ship and blasted it."]],[644,["That is such a strong rock that even now if you","have to nail them, you cannot put a drill on that."]],[650,["So, such a strong rock it is. And they","made such beautiful designs and things."]],[654,["But they blasted it. They were so much","against all these things, these Portuguese."]],[664,["So many temples, beautiful","temples they demolished."]],[667,["And the English also, terrible the English","were. English killed so many people in Calcutta."]],[673,["In a hole, they put them in a hole, known as","‘Hole of Calcutta’. And so many people were killed."]],[680,["Black hole of Calcutta."]],[680,["Black hole of Calcutta. And in Dhaka…"]],[684,["Jallianwala Bagh,"]],[686,["Jallianwala Bagh, another thing.","Just killed people just like that."]],[690,["In 1942."]],[692,["1942 yes, I was there."]],[696,["They put..."]],[697,["Yes, yes. They troubled","Me and tortured Me."]],[701,["They put Me on ice and all, they gave Me","electric shocks.  All of them know all about it."]],[710,["Horrible. They think they have a","right, you see to possess somebody."]],[714,["This is plundering, this is plundering. Go","to somebody’s country, take away everything,"]],[718,["plunder that person","and become the king?"]],[724,["Pirates, I tell you"]],[736,["Terrible thing they have done."]],[739,["But this killing people! Now, in Dhaka, there were","people who used to make beautiful ‘malmal’ , you see."]],[748,["A kind of a very thin cloth."]],[750,["Very beautiful cloth."]],[753,["So thin, they used to develop the nails."]],[756,["And in there was a little hole they used to","make. And out of that, they used to take out."]],[761,["It was a wonderful thing that one whole dhoti","could be put into a small little shell of a …"]],[773,["Walnut. Walnut"]],[775,["Walnut."]],[780,["The whole dhoti could","be put inside a walnut."]],[785,["And they killed them. All of them, they cut","their thumbs you see, they cut their thumbs."]],[792,["So jealous."]],[796,["Because the mills of Manchester","sell that cloth there."]],[799,["I mean, you cannot compete with","Manchester, because that was…this thing."]],[804,["But just an idea. It’s not that… you see, all of them. It's not English, the French, wherever they went, horrible."]],[811,["French have ruined so many people."]],[813,["Now, this Sierra Leone","where these people went."]],[819,["Actually, there are Australians working, but there","are the people who are there, are French, I think."]],[828,["The people who are ruling that place is","French. They are so cruel to these people,"]],[833,["that they have taken to Sahaja Yoga now."]],[838,["They’re extremely cruel."]],[841,["It’s there all the way","through that part of Africa."]],[847,["Portuguese were such","cruel people I tell you."]],[850,["Horrible.  Now they have become very poor."]],[854,["But all this white skin had that idea of aggressing","others, of plundering others, and sort of ruling everyone."]],[862,["Spanish."]],[864,["Spaniards are also bad. The whole of","America is covered by these Spaniards."]],[870,["I mean, they didn’t kill us so","much, the English, I must say,"]],[872,["the way they were killed by these","Spaniards for no reason at all."]],[878,["I went to this Rio de Janeiro,"]],[881,["and I wanted to see one aboriginal."]],[883,["One person was living there."]],[886,["They said, “We don’t have. You","can go in the museum and see.”"]],[889,["But not one single person left by these Spaniards' group."]],[893,["Now did you see the condition","of the Spanish, where are they?"]],[897,["In Brazil, Mother they still have..."]],[903,["it seems almost awful to say it, but they still have hunting parties where you can pay to go on a hunting party to shoot Indians."]],[918,["Shoot an Indian?"]],[920,["And the reason is money again, because they want to get them out of the forests so that they can go in and take the land."]],[928,["So they have safaris."]],[934,["And you know who, the","nation that goes the most?"]],[940,["The Germans."]],[941,["Oh!"]],[949,["Germans are very cunning. Now","they are all settled down there."]],[953,["This Argentina – that was the only time","I was happy that Argentina was defeated."]],[961,["Because all the Germans are there."]],[964,["They are teaching them all these things.","They are the ones who started the war."]],[967,["When I went to Argentina, we went for a navy parade"]],[974,["and I was surprised they were having those steps,","you see, goose steps they call them, like that."]],[980,["I said, I told My husband, “How are they","having goose steps, these Argentineans?”"]],[985,["He was also surprised you see","because these only Germans do."]],[990,["So when we asked them, they were shocked and","they said, “We have some German teachers.”"]],[994,["But all Germans who have run away from","the wartime are settled in Argentina."]],[999,["And they had big arrangements","to destroy the whole world."]],[1002,["So this has shattered; that’s the only point where","the British have done something very sensible."]],[1007,["Maybe I was in England –   very great –","that they have finished those Germans."]],[1013,["Though it has caused them a","lot of problems, no doubt."]],[1015,["But that was a sensible thing to do.","Because so many Germans have ruined"]],[1019,["– already building all kinds of things there."]],[1024,["In Paraguay, just north of there","too, there’s a lot of Germans."]],[1030,["But then the war between themselves."]],[1033,["Look at that."]],[1034,["Then the Germans start fighting them."]],[1037,["Germans didn’t go out, you","see, that is the thing is."]],[1041,["Germans did not fight the people outside","Europe or outside their territories."]],[1048,["What they wanted to fight is the English, the","Russians, all those people who are Europeans, there."]],[1056,["Polish."]],[1058,["So they started fight among themselves."]],[1061,["You see, violence is such that if you start","doing violence to anyone, it comes back to you."]],[1066,["And among yourselves, you start fighting."]],[1070,["And even now, Germans you cannot say."]],[1072,["They are like sleeping tigers."]],[1075,["I went to Germany Myself – West Germany","is all right, but East Germany I went to."]],[1080,["It’s like a… you feel like dead","cemeteries are everywhere."]],[1088,["But also through them, you feel there’s","a big violence building, even now."]],[1093,["They’re very hot-tempered, violent people."]],[1101,["You feel as if you have come into some hothouse."]],[1105,["Only once I went and I told C.P. I am not","going to come back again to this country:"]],[1110,["East Germany. Horrible!"]],[1114,["Even now the people are so hot-tempered."]],[1119,["Today if you… I tell you Russians","what they are doing it’s… thank God."]],[1124,["If you allow them to come up, they","can destroy the whole world."]],[1128,["They will try again too…"]],[1130,["Hitler could be born only in Germany. No other place."]],[1135,["Really!"]],[1136,["And there are many who worship Hitler even now."]],[1139,["Many. In East Germany, everyone. They","just say it was a political mistake."]],[1145,["That he attacked Russia?"]],[1150,["Same mistake as Napoleon made."]],[1153,["Yes, That’s what is the play. Krishna Leela is there."]],[1164,["But Germans – I mean they are the cruellest, I think."]],[1170,["No, the cruellest are the Japanese."]],[1172,["You can’t say because what I heard","about them in Warsaw, Warsaw."]],[1182,["They are so mean and so low-level. They took out the","fats of the people and used them for soap making."]],[1194,["That was in Hitler’s time."]],[1196,["Hitler’s time I am saying – Warsaw."]],[1198,["They made lampshades out","of their skin, Mother."]],[1202,["They used the skin."]],[1205,["And Jews are no less now."]],[1208,["Jews, they have picked up everything from Germans."]],[1211,["And the way they are now","torturing Palestinians."]],[1216,["Oh God, that’s also terrible."]],[1219,["They are taking the vengeance."]],[1221,["They were tortured at the hands of Hitler."]],[1225,["Now they are taking revenge from the Lebanese."]],[1231,["I don’t know it’s a revenge or a","kind of a thing what they saw in the war."]],[1236,["They became experts and they thought we must practise","now on Palestinians all those wretched things;"]],[1242,["whatever they have gone through."]],[1246,["There’s a lot of subtle things","that came out of Hitler."]],[1249,["Even though I know I shouldn’t,","every time I see the Swastika, I get…"]],[1256,["You get a fright."]],[1258,["You see, that is the lucky point."]],[1260,["What happened in Swastika,","Swastika is two ways."]],[1263,["One way is for construction, another","is for destruction: another side."]],[1269,["What happened, the trick of","the trade was like this;"]],[1272,["they were using stencils to make the Swastika."]],[1277,["And then they… one side they used and when they started","using the other side, it came out to be the other way round."]],[1284,["The wrong way."]],[1285,["It’s Swastika that defeated them."]],[1291,["(in Marathi): Swastika has two emblems. One","is constructive, the other is destructive."]],[1294,["If it is like this then it is constructive,","the opposite way is destructive."]],[1299,["They were using stencils. When it got damaged","on one side, they started using the other side."]],[1306,["When I saw them upside down, I said,","“Now finished. Now they are all right.”"]],[1313,["Hitler himself started","wearing upside-down thing."]],[1327,["And as he says, Japanese –","another. Another of this thing."]],[1332,["I was telling him the reason, because","in Japan, the mother is not respected."]],[1337,["Mother is just a dishwasher."]],[1339,["And the other women are geishas or dishwashers,","or, what you call them, career girls."]],[1346,["And the wives are dishwashers."]],[1349,["So the mother is always ill-treated, she is given","food outside, she doesn’t eat with the family;"]],[1354,["she’s treated just like a servant all the time."]],[1356,["She has to take out the shoes of","the husband, and she has to..."]],[1360,["I mean, do everything that a","maidservant has to do in the house."]],[1366,["So the children who see their mother being treated like","this develop that thing within themselves, that anger."]],[1372,["That’s why they are very angry people."]],[1374,["And the good-looking women","and career women never marry."]],[1379,["They never marry. And they never have children."]],[1383,["Because of this treatment?"]],[1385,["And the…If there is a very rich man, then he has","to pay a lot of money to marry a beautiful woman."]],[1391,["Then he marries her. But he goes to geisha house."]],[1394,["They will never take you to their houses, their homes."]],[1399,["If you see their women, their hands are like, just like washerwomen, you see, very rough and thick."]],[1407,["They sleep on the ground separately,","treated just like servants."]],[1413,["And they didn’t open their gates","for ages to any other country."]],[1417,["They lived with all that nonsense."]],[1419,["But Chinese are different. Chinese are like us."]],[1422,["Their whole system is like us, their styles are like","us, their whole morality sense is like us and also,"]],[1431,["they are very wise people.  Very wise."]],[1441,["See we have had another","problem I feel that way,"]],[1444,["that our Prime Ministers have been","all, you see Western-oriented:"]],[1449,["educated in the Western countries, except for Shastriji."]],[1454,["You see Balsar, this is the difference."]],[1459,["They never understood the value of our country."]],[1465,["More impressed by Western people."]],[1468,["Westernised people. Even this one."]],[1471,["He likes people who can speak","good English."]],[1476,["Even Rajiv Gandhi."]],[1479,["If they are Italians he likes them","more, because his wife is Italian."]],[1482,["I don’t know if he cares for that or not, but he","has very much inclination to a Westernised life."]],[1491,["Not that kind, but still."]],[1495,["That is one of the reasons, you see.","They are not children of the soil."]],[1499,["Except for Lal Bahadur Shastri, if he had lived,","we would have been a different country you see."]],[1505,["All dishonesty had vanished from","India, all corruption had vanished."]],[1509,["He was a very honest man.","Wonderful things were happening."]],[1513,["Corruption has come in. Honesty has","vanished and corruption has come in."]],[1520,["It has been impacted."]],[1523,["I think honesty is the one that opens the door","and lets corruption in though, isn’t it?"]],[1527,["That’s right."]],[1528,["You don’t expect people to be other than","honest; they open the door and in they come."]],[1535,["It is kind of a habit formation."]],[1538,["You see, get into the habit of getting money this way,","that way – then you start doing that all the time."]],[1543,["I think that must be the reason."]],[1545,["Because I have known people who were very good. Suddenly they become like that and they start grabbing this, grabbing that, grabbing that; there is no limit to things."]],[1553,["There should be certain maryadas for everything."]],[1561,["Yes, I find in Western societies,","maryadas is a thing that doesn’t exist."]],[1565,["Doesn’t exist in anything. In anything!"]],[1571,["It did."]],[1574,["It did. It did have. I mean,","they were reaching that point."]],[1577,["But before they could reach the Absolute, they","just got into this problem, of materialism."]],[1588,["How can you, see be a free person if you don’t respect","the freedom of another person? Maryada means that."]],[1595,["To respect the freedom of another person is maryadas."]],[1599,["And those maryadas one must have. Because of that,","you do not respect the freedom of another person."]],[1606,["You are aggressing each other all the time."]],[1609,["Whenever he has the chance, he will","aggress you or you will aggress him."]],[1612,["So it will go on like that, you see."]],[1615,["But if you respect the freedom of another","person, this is freedom and this is my freedom."]],[1620,["Then a maryada is put in there."]],[1624,["Then I suppose maryada means what","Christ said, “Do unto others…”"]],[1628,["As you want to be done to yourself."]],[1630,["Don’t hate."]],[1633,["But you see, they say that,","“Why? Why should we do that?”"]],[1637,["In England or in America or any of these places you","go to. You tell them, you should do. “But why?”"]],[1647,["But Christ has said it. “Who is Christ?”"]],[1649,["In America, they say. England,","they may not say so."]],[1652,["But America, they say, “Who is Christ?  Why","should we listen to?  Who is to tell us?”"]],[1661,["Abraham Lincoln is nothing for them."]],[1663,["You know there is only little","Lincoln Road somewhere far away."]],[1668,["They don’t regard him as anything great."]],[1673,["So what to do?"]],[1675,["They have a story about that also. An","American and a Russian were talking."]],[1680,["The American said that, “We","have such freedom in America"]],[1685,["that I can stand before the White House, the","President’s house and say that our President is a fool.”"]],[1692,["The Russian said, “I also can do that.”"]],[1696,["He said, “Really, is that so?”"]],[1698,["He said, “Yes, I can stand before your","President’s house and say that he is a fool.”"]],[1714,["But what I was telling him that, say in","Russia,"]],[1719,["restricted life is given to them. But no maryadas.","They don’t have maryadas, it’s only restricted life."]],[1725,["Now they are starting some sort","of a curtailing on drinking, say."]],[1731,["Now that will go on. But there is…"]],[1734,["It’s just by force, you see. Maryadas are","your own, ingrained.  It’s the culture."]],[1740,["So once they get out of that","place then they drink like hell."]],[1745,["Not that they’ve accepted","from within, those things"]],[1749,["that they are accepting these virtues","as a part and parcel of their being."]],[1753,["It’s just a force on them. So they are doing it."]],[1756,["But that day when they are","doing it, then they are Sahaj."]],[1759,["Sahaj, in a Sahaj way!  Maryadas","come to you in a Sahaj way."]],[1780,["It’s like tabla. Tabla."]],[1782,["Like tabla – it has to have a rhythm."]],[1787,["It cannot go on flowing with it."]],[1789,["You cannot just start it and go into any rhythm","or anything. You have to keep to that maryada."]],[1795,["In everything in life, there is maryada."]],[1800,["Otherwise, you wouldn’t know where you stand."]],[1802,["I mean, the sea also has a maryada."]],[1807,["The ocean has such a maryada"]],[1810,["that supposing you try to press the sea on one side","of the harbour, it will come out in some other part."]],[1819,["It starts showing in some other part."]],[1821,["But not beyond that."]],[1823,["Not beyond."]],[1824,["Supposing you try to raise the ..."]],[1827,["in Bombay they have done it, you see. They have raised","Bombay in these areas like say, Marine Drive and all that."]],[1836,["It has shown in other places."]],[1845,["In Versova, the sea has entered the land."]],[1850,["It keeps to its maryadas."]],[1856,["And it is such an uncertain society."]],[1860,["If you don’t have maryadas, you don’t","know how you stand with another person."]],[1865,["You cannot find out your relationships","with each other, you see."]],[1868,["You cannot understand how far","you can go with that person."]],[1872,["It’s a very funny stuff, not to have maryadas."]],[1879,["I suppose"]],[1882,["one of the problems in Western society","is that we have been taught to believe"]],[1886,["that you can’t have maryadas, because if you want","to get on in this world in a business sense,"]],[1893,["you have to find some way of doing","something better than someone else,"]],[1898,["which means that you have to tread on","them to get higher up on the ladder."]],[1902,["But that can be done with maryadas also."]],[1907,["You see, doing better than other means","what?  Must have maryadas, isn’t it."]],[1913,["Supposing there are two","persons who are doing business."]],[1917,["One person tries to outwit another person by","false means or sort of, all kinds of other things."]],[1924,["Luring him into something funny"]],[1927,["like taking him to women, then do this and do","that. All sorts of wrong things he takes to."]],[1934,["How far will he go?"]],[1940,["But a person who goes in his maryadas can transcend","everyone else, because he has kept his personality intact."]],[1948,["He has not wasted it,","frittered away or made it cheap."]],[1956,["And the idea of doing better","is also money-oriented."]],[1963,["But doing better in a general way is different."]],[1966,["Like, I will tell you. Lal Bahadur Shastri was a man; when there was an accident, a railway accident in the South. He resigned."]],[1979,["Means he was the Minister of Railways."]],[1981,["He had nothing to do with that railway in","particular or anything, but he resigned."]],[1986,["Just resigned."]],[1988,["“When I am the Railway Minister and if there is an","accident, I should not be the minister.” He just resigned."]],[1994,["And everybody remembers it and tells","about it, “See now what he has done.”"]],[1998,["He had that maryadas."]],[2001,["And there are many other railway ministers we have","had who made money, did all this and everything."]],[2005,["People don’t want to take their names in the morning","time. “No God, no, don’t take their names in the morning.”"]],[2013,["I don’t think we’ve got too many","politicians who would do that."]],[2015,["They would have fifty-four reasons as","to why it was someone else’s fault."]],[2022,["Like Shivaji’s case, I will tell you one","thing. Shivaji was a man of great maryadas."]],[2027,["Shivaji’s people once looted a big treasures of a","“subedar,” Kalyan subedar and his daughter-in-law."]],[2037,["She was going and with her,","all her treasures were going."]],[2039,["Very beautiful woman… and they brought her. And she came with her covering on her face, you see."]],[2046,["Veil."]],[2047,["Ah, veil."]],[2049,["And she was presented to Shivaji."]],[2055,["So Shivaji asked her that, “You open your veil.”"]],[2061,["She opened her veil."]],[2063,["So, he said…he saluted","her and he said, “See now,"]],[2067,["if my mother was as beautiful as you are, I would","have been even more beautiful than you are.”"]],[2074,["What a beautiful thing to say!","You see, sisterly relationship."]],[2078,["“If my mother was as beautiful as you are, I","would have been even more beautiful than you.”"]],[2083,["And he shouted at all his subedars and all that.","“Don’t do all such things. No insults to women.”"]],[2089,["And he sent her back with all the things","that she was carrying, plus his own…"]],[2095,["with his own army to leave, to be left up to the","place where she was… from where she had come."]],[2102,["Man of such maryadas, you see."]],[2105,["He never felt anything attractive or anything about her. He","just felt, “A sweet sister of mine, such a beautiful sister."]],[2113,["If I was…if my mother was as beautiful as she","is, I would have been as beautiful as this.”"]],[2118,["Just a sisterly feeling, to","come to a man of maryadas."]],[2123,["And he was forced to marry four times by his mother because you see, they had to do some sort of a pact with other people."]],[2132,["So he had to marry four times."]],[2135,["Imagine."]],[2135,["He married four times because","mother asked him, but in maryadas."]],[2139,["But when he saw such a beautiful","woman, he just told her."]],[2146,["Always he spent his life","in the company of saints."]],[2150,["Always."]],[2153,["Such maryadas, you see; in a","saint also, there are maryadas."]],[2158,["Like a saint, like Tukarama."]],[2161,["He went and saw him, and he saw the condition he","was... Tukarama was in a very poor condition."]],[2166,["So he brought a lot of ornaments and everything and gave","it to his wife and lots of food and all that in the house."]],[2175,["So Tukarama came back and he told his wife that.","And Shivaji was hearing what Tukarama had to say."]],[2183,["He said, “See, this is meant for","queens and kings, not for us."]],[2187,["We are poor farmers, and it doesn’t behove for","a farmer to wear all these expensive things."]],[2195,["So you better return all this to Shivaji.”"]],[2198,["Shivba, Shivba they used to call him Shivba."]],[2200,["“But you see, whatever is suitable for your status, you wear","that. That will look nice on you, this you better give. ”"]],[2209,["And he was surprised. But Shivaji was there. He","came and fell at his feet, so he gave..."]],[2222,["Excuse me Shri Mataji, I think","Your dinner would be ready soon."]],[2228,["What time we have to go?"]],[2231,["It’s about ten minutes drive","Mother, just down the street."]],[2234,["And what time is the program?"]],[2235,["Programme is for seven-thirty…"]],[2238,["Seven-thirty."]],[2239,["so we will be there from seven o clock, maybe…"]],[2241,["So if you think proper, I’ll come back and have","dinner, because I am really not at all hungry. Alright?"]],[2247,["I’ll have some tea, that’s all."]],[2250,["There is a note from… you know a K.C. Meddapa?"]],[2254,["Auh?"]],[2255,["K.C. Madappa? From India. K.C…"]],[2261,["Madappa."]],[2264,["Well, his sister is here, Mother. Sister’s","name is Daya. She wishes an audience with you."]],[2271,["She’s a doctor."]],[2274,["She says that you know this K.C."]],[2276,["Of course!"]],[2278,["We didn’t know whether it was someone that was","just saying that they knew You when they didn’t."]],[2286,["Madappa. Madappa was","secretary of Sanjeeva Reddy."]],[2292,["He has seen Me curing Sanjeeva","Reddy and also curing so many people."]],[2296,["Madappa. A friend of C.P.","Oh, I would love to see him."]],[2301,["Actually it’s his sister."]],[2303,["His sister, yes."]],[2306,["Yes, Doctor Ganapati,","who is the sister of K.C."]],[2309,["So when would she like to see Me?"]],[2312,["Well, we have a telephone","number here, we could ring her."]],[2314,["And whenever she is free, ask her. Whenever she","is free. See, tomorrow is a programme, isn’t it?"]],[2324,["Tomorrow night, but tomorrow is free – tomorrow day."]],[2328,["Sorry! It’s eleven o’clock, is it?"]],[2330,["Eleven o’clock what?"]],[2331,["There’s a newspaper man…"]],[2334,["A person coming, eleven o’clock. Then, before that?"]],[2340,["How about after two?"]],[2343,["Or we can have it about... before the programme","tomorrow? Day after we are going, aren’t we?"]],[2351,["No wait. We are going on Friday,","so tomorrow is Wednesday."]],[2356,["Then she can see Me on Thursday morning."]],[2360,["Thursday morning."]],[2362,["Thursday we will go out for shopping","a little bit, I was thinking."]],[2365,["Ah, wonderful."]],[2367,["Because I want to show","him also some things here."]],[2370,["You make one thing, in that you get in Melbourne,","the same thing I was telling you about."]],[2374,["Yes, Shri Mataji."]],[2375,["That’s something you make. I have discovered","four/five things you make in Melbourne."]],[2385,["And you wanted to see Kerry","too, Mother, sometime. Kerry?"]],[2388,["I want to see him also, Kerry also. I want to see him,","yes. So should we try on him after the programme, anytime."]],[2397,["Thank you Shri Mataji."]],[2400,["Day after tomorrow?  After the programme."]],[2409,["There’s still time, a lot of time."]],[2418,["I don’t know when this started –","taking money in the name of God."]],[2424,["A long time ago I think, Mother."]],[2426,["But Martin Luther, who was a realised","soul, he flouted Mister Pope completely."]],[2434,["And he brought him to task."]],[2437,["But then again these same people","have taken the same sort of a thing."]],[2445,["I’ve often wondered whether Paul","used to take money on the side."]],[2449,["I’ll bet he did. I am sure he did."]],[2454,["Paul, Mother!"]],[2455,["I never cared for Mister Paul."]],[2458,["And somebody bought a couple","of new horses or something."]],[2461,["He must be. Must be. He was not connected with God, he must be. You see, he must have changed his role just to make money."]],[2467,["Otherwise, why did he become Christian?"]],[2469,["That’s what I thought. There must","have been a reason for all this."]],[2474,["But he was hanged later on you","know. He was hanged ultimately."]],[2481,["I’m sure he always had the latest horse Mother."]],[2484,["Like you have the latest car, he","always had the newest horse, I’m sure."]],[2487,["Latest car. But I must say one thing, that","people are also extremely, extremely stupid."]],[2495,["‘They’re gullible’"]],[2496,["They get what they deserve. I went to Boston, I think, yes."]],[2502,["And they asked Me a question, the TV","people, “How many Rolls Royces She has?”"]],[2509,["That time Rajneesh was on the top you see."]],[2512,["So they said, “She has no Rolls Royces. She","takes no money.\"  He said, \"We’re not interested.”"]],[2518,["It’s a business you see."]],[2524,["But of course, Mother the television","industry itself is a business,"]],[2529,["and if they think there’s  no selling","property in whatever it is that they…"]],[2536,["Yes"]],[2537,["we offer them, then they don’t want to know,","because they are selling advertising space."]],[2542,["That’s not their responsibility there."]],[2545,["Television and all these things came on this","earth, you can see from the photographs;"]],[2550,["the whole electrical energy was manifested in","the brains of human beings for Sahaja Yoga."]],[2560,["Even if they accept or not,"]],[2563,["they must know that it is for","Sahaja Yog, for spreading Sahaja Yoga,"]],[2567,["because Christ came, that time there were very few people, they could not spread Christianity, so well."]],[2573,["They did all this mess out of it."]],[2575,["But now there is television."]],[2579,["They have been ringing all day today Mother, saying,","“We saw that lady on the television last week."]],[2585,["When is She speaking in","Melbourne?”  Hundreds of them."]],[2588,["Really?"]],[2591,["There’s one little television","programme it just keeps going."]],[2594,["And it will be the same in Adelaide,","because they saw it there too."]],[2598,["Same?"]],[2599,["Yes, they saw that programme all around Australia,","every capital city and a lot of smaller cities."]],[2605,["There were telephone calls from Townsville,","right up in the north of Australia;"]],[2611,["from Perth, from Adelaide, from Canberra."]],[2616,["All these places saw You."]],[2619,["And have you not had time to tell Mother","the incredible story of the school…."]],[2629,["Mother, I have something. I","go to a teacher’s college…"]],[2634,["Yes?"]],[2634,["To learn how to be a teacher"]],[2635,["Yes?"]],[2636,["And one of the subjects we were doing","yesterday was Psychology in Education."]],[2641,["So, one man, who is a psychologist for twenty-five","years, he is teaching us how to understand our students"]],[2648,["and his remedy for relaxing is to take one","bottle of alcohol at home and drink."]],[2655,["That’s what he is teaching us at school."]],[2659,["Anyway, yesterday I had some of your posters","to do at the school, to put up at the school"]],[2666,["and I was sitting there for two hours."]],[2668,["We were talking about what is intellect, how","good the ego is, and how to enhance the ego."]],[2679,["The ego must take you on."]],[2681,["So I was sort of going [Yogi gestures","something] sleeping like this"]],[2686,["and there was one other girl in the class. A very","simple girl from up the country and she said,"]],[2692,["\"Excuse me Mr Sullivan, is what you're talking about ego? Is this sort of left side, female, past and right side male, future action?"]],[2707,["And sort of Ego and, well Ego and","Superego or somewhere up there?”"]],[2714,["And I listened and it was Sahaj","she was speaking."]],[2718,["And the psychologist said, “No, no, no","that’s all wrong. That’s all wrong."]],[2724,["Erm, from the left side, we learn how to write and from the right side, we learn how to read. That’s what you’re talking about.” finished."]],[2734,["So I went to her after and I said, “Do you want to know","about the left side and the desire, the pure desire of God,"]],[2742,["and the pure action of God and how we can do this, and the balance and the centre channel?” She said, “Yes. Do you know about that?”"]],[2750,["I said, “Yes, I do. I have it here.”","And I showed her one of Your pictures."]],[2755,["And she said, “That’s Her. That’s","the Lady there. That’s the Lady.”"]],[2760,["And I said, “Where did you see Her?”","And she said, “On television.”"]],[2765,["And she’s coming tonight and tomorrow night."]],[2769,["That must be… well we know there are","millions of people watched that programme."]],[2773,["Charles told Me now, “So many have seen","You Mother. That’s the biggest thing"]],[2777,["they have seen You, that’s the biggest thing. So","happy with this idea, that they have seen You.”"]],[2785,["What a wonderful thing television","will be, as you say, for Sahaja Yoga."]],[2789,["When we can get time, we don’t have to fight","our way in, because it’s so much easier."]],[2796,["It just goes straight out."]],[2797,["Even loudspeaker you will be","surprised is of such a help."]],[2801,["You see, what had happened, I used to speak and Raolbai told Me that she sees vibrations, “going from this, Mother.”"]],[2809,["I said, “Really?”  She said, “Yes, they go into this.”"]],[2812,["“So then let’s try one thing.”  Then","I started blowing into it. That works."]],[2822,["That means whenever I speak also it opens out."]],[2832,["This television man got it afterwards but I don’t","know if he is going to announce that or say that."]],[2838,["He wants to see me when I go back to Sydney."]],[2840,["He asked me out to lunch but I couldn’t go because I","had to come here. But I know he wants to talk about it."]],[2848,["Maybe we could get him for Ayers Rock – for Uluru, for Ganesha Puja in ‘88. Line it up for then. It would be wonderful."]],[2859,["Yes could be. Already your group","will be very big I think so."]],[2871,["But this I told on the television, this","left and right? I must have said it."]],[2876,["Yes, she said she heard it from You."]],[2878,["In that short time."]],[2882,["So at least the audience watching at home","was much better than the studio audience.."]],[2886,["They’re all loosely dressing up, all the time","looking after the dress and grinning at the thing."]],[2892,["You see, I was watching them; they were very self-conscious."]],[2895,["Oh yes!"]],[2896,["They knew the camera was on them."]],[2897,["Ah, that’s it. So, they were not for this","programme at all. None of them were seekers."]],[2907,["It’s quite funny Mother, with…"]],[2910,["Even with a microphone, if you","have somebody who talks a lot,"]],[2914,["they go, “la, la, la…” the whole time,"]],[2916,["you put the microphone in front of them and","they go, “Uhh…” and they can’t say a word."]],[2921,["Because suddenly…"]],[2922,["(Marathi): You should go out and walk around."]],[2924,["You can take him around a","little. Let him have a look."]],[2926,["(Marathi): After, I will rest for a while."]],[2929,["(Marathi): All right. Take a rest."]],[2930,["So?"]],[2932,["It is amazing how self-conscious they get the","moment you put a microphone in front of somebody"]],[2937,["or put a camera there in front of them and bang! They can","think of nothing else except, “Everybody’s looking at me!”"]],[2943,["Really?"]],[2944,["Yes, everything goes …"]],[2947,["Yes, that’s something. Self-consciousness."]],[2959,["We have a saying which is, you don’t need to worry","about what other people are thinking about you."]],[2964,["Because they are not thinking about you,"]],[2966,["they’re worrying about what other","people are thinking about them."]],[2972,["It’s the truth."]],[2975,["Ah, it is very true."]],[2979,["Rustom and these two have gone somewhere?"]],[2982,["(in Hindi): They are sleeping."]],[2984,["They are sleeping? Both of them?"]],[2988,["They never had their dinner or what?"]],[2991,["We had biscuits and cheese","and tea and talk and…"]],[2995,["Then Rustom went for a walk and Rajesh Shah is asleep. The food was already… it was dished up and we had to take it back."]],[3002,["They are tired, I think. Yeah?"]],[3008,["And everybody else now is outside at the","railway station giving out the handbills"]],[3013,["Handbills and all that, yes."]],[3016,["It’s been very successful, the handbills, Mother."]],[3018,["Handbills and also posters","are very successful."]],[3020,["Very good, the handbills."]],[3022,["But television is just for Me, nothing else. I mean, I can give","realisation on television to people, if they give Me at chance and time."]],[3030,["But the way they, you see, just put you on the","seat and then you are out – jack in the box"]],[3034,["they’ll just throw you out and then another","person comes and sits. It’s just impossible."]],[3046,["Still it’s bringing a lot of people to Your programmes."]],[3049,["Also Sahaja Yoga is a very sensible","thing itself. It works out."]],[3053,["Like, as many as people you have, you see, it","will get the people that you can balance also."]],[3059,["It goes on balancing. And it doesn’t","give you too much of a load also."]],[3063,["If you have too much of a","load, how will you manage them?"]],[3067,["That’s right. This is one of the things","that I’ve always looked at with wonder"]],[3071,["how, over the years here in Australia as we have grown,","so we have got a few more. But we never had too many."]],[3078,["Too many, yes. You came to","Melbourne only first time, did you?"]],[3083,["Oh no, I was here before, the last time."]],[3085,["No, no, no but when you got your","realisation, where did you get it?"]],[3090,["You got it in Sydney. But in Melbourne,","lots of people came here in ’82, I think."]],[3096,["I think yes, they came down from…","the original lot came from Sydney."]],[3101,["Oh, I see"]],[3102,["And then they transferred."]],[3104,["Spread out, yes."]],[3107,["That’s when I first met You, Mother."]],[3109,["You met Me here?"]],[3111,["Yes. You came…that was my house that you came and","stopped in, in Essendon – the very first visit."]],[3117,["The very first visit, there’s","a small wooden house there."]],[3120,["Of course, I remember him very well."]],[3123,["Because he came to receive us and he took us down to","his house, which was a small little house, I remember."]],[3130,["Everything I remember very clearly, that part."]],[3136,["But that time he was not listening","about Sahaja Yoga so much."]],[3142,["I was pretty stupid then, Mataji."]],[3146,["We tell some funny stories about that."]],[3150,["But I got round him. I could see that","he’s a seeker but he’s lost his way."]],[3157,["So I took a lot of interest in him."]],[3163,["No, those who came first, always go wrong. Something","goes wrong with them, you see. Horrible they are."]],[3170,["One better than the other. I mean","I don’t know how to address that."]],[3175,["Everywhere it has happened. Even a","person like Gregoire has lost his head."]],[3184,["That's surprised how it happens."]],[3188,["He was quite shocked but then he realised,","he confessed it to Me, “Mother, it happens.”"]],[3195,["Brent and I were driving somewhere up North about three","weeks ago, and we were adding up the number of original…"]],[3203,["Sahaja Yogis."]],[3205,["There weren’t many. We began to get worried."]],[3209,["Yes, yes, it happens."]],[3211,["It makes us very cautious: be careful."]],[3218,["The…In London also, I gave realisation to some few before."]],[3224,["I mean, the first batches that were."]],[3227,["Gradually, surprisingly they became quite funny, and they","started an organisation called “The old Sahaja Yogis.”"]],[3238,["I didn’t know that. Suddenly I","found the behaviour rather funny."]],[3244,["I said, “What is this going on?” They","said, “We are old Sahaja Yogis.”"]],[3247,["“Alright, better be seated now for your old age.”"]],[3259,["Because you see, all these are ideas."]],[3262,["Some person who comes today might rise very fast."]],[3266,["Somebody who might have come from long","– you have seen it, what happened."]],[3272,["Some people stay still, a lot."]],[3274,["Quite a few, don’t they? You","talk about them and they..."]],[3279,["you think, well, I’ve been here five","years, six years whatever it is"]],[3282,["and that person’s exactly the same as when I first","met them– they haven’t changed one little bit."]],[3288,["That’s it. So what do you say to that?"]],[3291,["And even if you pass ten","years you will be the same."]],[3296,["So what is most important is","how far you grow, is the point."]],[3301,["That growth is very important."]],[3303,["And this leadership or anything,","whatever it is, is not so important."]],[3308,["How far you grow. As soon as","you grow, your light will grow."]],[3321,["And some people I have seen, have","come to Sahaja Yoga very, very late."]],[3327,["They have shot up like anything."]],[3330,["And some people who have been there... I mean, there are two brothers and sisters, like Nirmala’s brother and herself."]],[3339,["There is a contrast I should say."]],[3343,["Contrast. If you see the brother you will be amazed."]],[3345,["I know  Prabakh and he is very good, Mother."]],[3348,["He is tremendous. He is very deep"]],[3353,["I think I detect another thing with looking back, I see,","as the collective has got bigger, people develop quicker."]],[3364,["That’s very important – collective is very","important. Collective is the nourishing garden."]],[3370,["Helps a lot. Yes."]],[3371,["Now supposing you try this experiment. If","there is a tree that is dying, you see."]],[3377,["Now, you bring other trees next to it, it will grow."]],[3382,["With a pot you see, little pot you can have where the flowers are dying. Bring it near the other pots which are healthy, it will grow."]],[3391,["Normally it happens like this,"]],[3393,["that if you have one bad apple,","all the good apples will be spoilt."]],[3397,["All their goodness cannot put that right, you see."]],[3400,["That’s it. But with the growth, it happens."]],[3405,["If something is living and","growing. If somebody is dead,"]],[3409,["then, of course, the decaying is much faster."]],[3413,["But if somebody is living and growing, with","the more healthier people it grows faster."]],[3419,["And isn’t it interesting Mother, how when somebody in the collective gets sick, the first thing they want to do is to move out."]],[3428,["It is true?"]],[3432,["It is true, yes absolutely."]],[3435,["It is almost as though they want to commit","suicide and just about want to destroy themselves."]],[3440,["Who?"]],[3440,["Almost as if they want to destroy themselves."]],[3442,["Yes."]],[3443,["By moving out. Moving away."]],[3448,["That’s a typical example."]],[3459,["So many experiments you will be","doing, more and more and more"]],[3461,["and you will be amazed at the results."]],[3466,["Very much."]],[3468,["Sahaja Yoga is such an enterprise I should","say. Every day you discover something new,"]],[3475,["every day you find out something","new, that you can manage."]],[3479,["Like the flowers! The miracle of the flowers!"]],[3486,["Michael’s breadboard, Mother."]],[3487,["Huh?"]],[3488,["That piece of wood that you pushed the flowers down","was his breadboard, Mother that he cuts the bread on."]],[3494,["Oh, I see!"]],[3495,["He’s never going to use it again."]],[3497,["I have put it away in my bedroom, Mother."]],[3502,["We couldn’t find anything to do that. You see"]],[3504,["I said they must be little bit dipped in","the water. Because I had vibrated the water."]],[3510,["This was very cold water so I said, “Alright, let’s make","it little warm or hot.” They said, “The flowers will die.”"]],[3515,["I said, “No, My hand is there. That will cool it down.”"]],[3519,["And all the flowers survived, all of them. And","they came up so well and they grew in size."]],[3525,["Yes, they did. And Mother, was it the heat","from the body that killed the flowers or…"]],[3532,["Heat from the body!"]],[3533,["Why did the flowers start to die?"]],[3536,["Because of the heat from your bodies. You see,","there was too much heat you were passing in the body."]],[3541,["While I put them in the water and I","vibrated the water, you see with My hand."]],[3546,["So you see, I may be perspiring Myself but","I emit cool breeze. Ask him, he saw that."]],[3552,["Oh yes, We went shopping, and Mother was","perspiring because it was very hot in the shop"]],[3557,["and I was helping Mother down the stairs."]],[3560,["And all of a sudden, this “whoosh” came","over. I said “Mother, it can’t be!”"]],[3565,["And his wife too. “See, Mother such","cool breeze you are giving us.”"]],[3568,["It just swept over us"]],[3569,["So I was cooling all of you and taking the heat","within Myself. It is like an air conditioner you see."]],[3575,["That gets heated up and makes everything cool."]],[3581,["Just like the back of fridge is very hot."]],[3584,["Fridge is very hot. If you see the back","of it, yes that’s hot, that’s what it is."]],[3590,["Even sometimes My tongue emits so much of heat I feel,","outside – the heat is going out in the night time."]],[3597,["But if you put your finger around My nose in","the night, it is a very cool breeze coming."]],[3610,["I wish Christ had told more about Holy","Ghost.  He had time to talk about it."]],[3620,["Do you think, Mother that we have been told all that","Christ talked about or that it’s been a little bit lost?"]],[3628,["Lot of it must have been lost because I am sure","He must have told about Kundalini and all that."]],[3634,["But you see the disciples were not","realised until He lived, as you know that."]],[3640,["And they were a very uncertain quantity."]],[3643,["They were very frightened because He was crucified"]],[3646,["and they couldn’t say that a man who was God","has been crucified by human beings, you see."]],[3652,["How to prove that He was God is that."]],[3656,["Matthews was very much frightened of saying","something about Immaculate Conception."]],[3664,["There was a big fight between him","and Paul because he outlasted Christ."]],[3670,["And he wouldn’t say that – Paul would not say. In his","books, he has not mentioned a word about all this."]],[3676,["But Matthews was forced by other disciples","that we must write whatever we have seen."]],[3683,["So the whole thing became here like a, little … we","should say, a loose organisation between them,"]],[3693,["and they wrote whatever","they felt like in the Bible,"]],[3696,["but not what... John was enthusiastic and","young fellow. So he wrote lots of things."]],[3702,["In that – as a dream or anything, or whatever it is,","but he wrote many things, which is quite good."]],[3715,["But still, a lot of it’s missing because Christ","could not have missed those points; I am sure of it."]],[3720,["Most of them just couldn’t write, could they?"]],[3723,["Only Luke and Matthew would have been probably the only two who could write; I don’t know whether John could write."]],[3729,["John could write also."]],[3732,["But Matthew used to write really well."]],[3734,["They were all fishermen. Ordinary people of ordinary intelligence."]],[3741,["How far can you talk to them about Kundalini also?"]],[3744,["But I am sure Christ must have told","them that there’s  a force within you."]],[3748,["That he must have told them. He","must have told them everything."]],[3752,["And that is why when the cool breeze came to them,","you see, they felt that it is the Holy Ghost."]],[3762,["Otherwise, they could not have related it to that."]],[3764,["They must have known. Very","haphazard, the whole thing was."]],[3773,["Also, like Christ made the wine. Now wine was in","those days not taken like the way we take it;"]],[3781,["it was called as ‘strong drinks’ and its","brew was prohibited: actually prohibited."]],[3786,["If you read Moses, He has prohibited strong drinks clearly."]],[3791,["But that was not Christ’s realm to talk","about. But still, He never made, you see"]],[3796,["wine, which we call as wine nowadays, alcoholic,","because alcohol cannot be made in one minute."]],[3807,["That’s the point one should see. You see He..","it was… He made wine means He made the juice."]],[3812,["Tastes like wine."]],[3814,["The other day this Romano fellow: I asked him,","“You first take something,” because they all drink."]],[3821,["So, he is the fan of the Italian","people, you know, the one who did Me."]],[3827,["So he said, “You first you give me realisation.”"]],[3830,["So I put My hand in the thing and","I said, “Now you drink this water.”"]],[3836,["He said, “This is water?”"]],[3838,["He asked the girl. “Yeah.” “You brought","water?” “Yes, I brought water.”"]],[3842,["He said, “No, this tastes like wine.” I","said, “Go ahead, drink.” Then he drank."]],[3857,["And then also many things happened with","him because he arranged a programme,"]],[3863,["a big programme in Italy in a place where they","have a very expensive holiday camping place."]],[3871,["They call it the Santa Pietra."]],[3876,["Pietra is the stone, you see where there is a saint that is a stone;"]],[3882,["means must be some sort","of a swayambhu there."]],[3886,["So we went there, to that...","Marina Santa Pietra is the place."]],[3891,["And there he had a big programme in a big palace,","which had a very big open-air theatre and all that."]],[3899,["There he had the programme."]],[3901,["But he told Me, “I’m sorry, but everybody has told me you","can’t have the programme, it’s going to rain cats and dogs."]],[3908,["It’s going to have a very bad… also maybe","snowfall or maybe something like that.”"]],[3914,["I told him, “No, not possible. There","will be no rain at all, believe Me.”"]],[3920,["So we had Alganesh and Alganesh said,","“If Mother says so, we believe it.”"]],[3925,["He said, “My faith is not that strong as yours.”","I said, “Alright, but just try it once.”"]],[3931,["So Gregoire and all these people","had come from outside that area."]],[3935,["They said, “Till we came inside the city, it was raining"]],[3939,["there was hailstorm, all things happening,","we thought we won’t be able to reach."]],[3944,["It's not clear cut.”"]],[3946,["Then they came, and we had in the evening the programme.","It was absolutely clear sky: absolutely clear sky."]],[3955,["And about six miles away from there, it was","raining, there was hailstorm all around."]],[3961,["And the programme went off very well."]],[3963,["So, in the beginning, only he said that, “The first miracle","is this; that She had told me there will not be any  rain,"]],[3970,["and everybody I telephoned, they said, “There’s","going to be rain. Take a bet on that.”"]],[3982,["A very nice man and it was very interesting in the way the whole programme came up, so many people got realisation."]],[3991,["In Italy now it is quite established. Especially","in Milano areas, it is very much established."]],[4000,["Italians are not so fond of","Pope; they have had enough of him."]],[4003,["He has got six thousand schools all over Italy.","And very highly paid schools. Very highly paid."]],[4010,["And nobody gets admissions there easily."]],[4013,["It is a very big money racket."]],[4015,["All those things they know. And they were saying that","every day there are six to seven thousand visitors"]],[4023,["and every visitor has to pay so much money when","he goes around, just for visiting the Vatican."]],[4029,["All that he is earning every day."]],[4032,["Such are his earnings, everything and I have seen he has really, tremendous amount of treasury: tremendous amount."]],[4040,["Even more than Tsars, and he doesn’t want to sell it."]],[4044,["And while Italians were saying, that","we are so poor, that time."]],[4049,["And also you see, all the","Catholics are very poor."]],[4052,["Now, Italian things have improved."]],[4056,["They asked Me for one thing – is mafia is to be","completely finished. That thing has happened now in Italy."]],[4063,["Also that their poverty should go.","Now they have become very rich people."]],[4074,["I had an aunt, Mother who lived just","north of Milan – in Como, on the lake."]],[4081,["Really? We had a program there, in Como."]],[4084,["It’s a beautiful place."]],[4085,["And such a big, huge hall – bigger","than yours, all filled with people."]],[4090,["And one priest came and he started saying,","“Thank Mother for She has given us our light,"]],[4096,["She has given us our","Self-realisation.” I was amazed."]],[4099,["A priest?"]],[4100,["Priest."]],[4102,["That is extraordinary."]],[4109,["Because he is a priest, Sahaja","Yogis don’t allow him to come."]],[4113,["They said, “You better change your dress, otherwise, we","won’t allow you to come.” I did not say anything about it."]],[4121,["There you can do it because Sahaja","Yoga is very much established."]],[4135,["So who is this psychologist who was teaching there?"]],[4139,["What sort of a school?"]],[4140,["It’s the teachers' college","Mother, for technical teachers."]],[4145,["So I teach cooking, you know for the","trade – for the technical trade"]],[4152,["and we have plumbers, hairdressers,","pastry makers, cooks, electricians,"]],[4164,["and all we who teach have to then go to school","two days a week to learn how to teach further."]],[4171,["So these are very big teachers that teach the teachers."]],[4175,["But how… he is teaching psychology to you people also?"]],[4178,["Yes he is. yes. Psychology in education!"]],[4182,["It is supposed to let me know what","happens inside the students’ heads."]],[4189,["He shouldn’t be doing the teaching."]],[4191,["What happens? But I mean, you are feeding the stomach","and the tongue – it never goes to the head, does it?"]],[4201,["I think any cooking done with","love turns out to be good food."]],[4211,["Yeah."]],[4216,["And every country has its own style","because it suits them that way, you see."]],[4221,["Whatever suits that country, they have to take it."]],[4227,["So now it’s done?"]],[4230,["Alright? May God Bless You."]],[4238,["There is something I wanted to tell you both."]],[4242,["It is a little personal."]],[4245,["You see, our great Mr David has married an Australian","girl, and like all other Englishmen, he doesn’t talk."]],[4254,["So she says he doesn’t communicate."]],[4258,["So I told that, “Englishmen don’t talk","much, you see."]],[4261,["They allow others to talk. They","listen more than talk themselves."]],[4264,["So you don’t get upset – you go on talking to him, he will","listen to you, and he’ll say few words to you in any case.”"]],[4270,["So I am just to going to warn you","people, you are marrying outside."]],[4274,["Especially in America, they talk a lot, you see.","So just don’t keep quiet. You have to talk."]],[4282,["If they say something you better talk. And","you have to start talking sometimes also."]],[4286,["Because David really shocked Me."]],[4289,["He said, “Really? I communicate all right, Mother.”"]],[4293,["He was quite surprised."]],[4295,["I said, “He is a quiet fellow.","That’s all, he’s a little quiet.”"]],[4301,["That’s the way they are; the English don’t talk much."]],[4306,["I think it’s more that if you think the things… you think you’ve said them without actually saying, without actually communicating."]],[4317,["But mentally, you feel you’re communicating, because  I used to find that with people thought that…"]],[4322,["I used to think that I was very quiet… that I spoke","a lot, but actually it was just going on in my head"]],[4329,["and it wasn’t actually, wasn’t actually really","communication, it was just in my own mind"]],[4335,["In your  head, you were talking."]],[4337,["Must be.  You better tell David."]],[4340,["You know, because poor David, he","didn’t know what was wrong with him."]],[4345,["He’s a quiet fellow. He lived","in My house for a year or so."]],[4350,["Quiet. You see, tell him something, he’ll do that."]],[4353,["BREAK IN RECORDING"]],[4354,["with Gorbachev and your America."]],[4356,["I mean she is a small country, now come down to your level and don’t tell people that, “We are British, British, British.”"]],[4362,["And all the money is drained off, you see."]],[4365,["It’s so much trouble to these people, you know."]],[4368,["Young people are really become","poor there. No jobs, nothing."]],[4372,["All the money is going to missiles. What","are you going to do with these few missiles?"]],[4378,["Hopefully nothing!"]],[4382,["It’s terrible, terrible the way things are happening there."]],[4385,["You see, I feel sometimes","that this lady has no heart."]],[4388,["Like a mother to think about her children.","(British Prime Minister, Margaret Thatcher)"]],[4390,["So many young people are unemployed.","She is not bothered about unemployment."]],[4395,["How these things come in? Because","of unemployment: drugs or anything."]],[4401,["They have nothing to do poor things, what can they","do? What is their future? She is not bothered"]],[4411,["And now what she’s done? She has","done, is open the, you see, the market."]],[4416,["This whole thing is open now. Anybody can go","and this bull and this stuff has started there."]],[4422,["Is all open; anybody can do what they","like. So the pound has gone up."]],[4428,["Anybody can go and join the stock exchange.","So, yesterday the thing has gone up."]],[4437,["The pound is up, alright.  But what’s the use?"]],[4444,["The pound has gone up but it’s no","good to you if you haven’t got any."]],[4448,["It is artificially. It is not really."]],[4451,["Because she has allowed people to take","their loans, as much as they want."]],[4455,["Then another thing she has done; a very dangerous thing"]],[4457,["that whatever is the income out of the factories, she wants","to distribute them as bonuses to all the shareholders."]],[4469,["So the factories will become","tomorrow very weak also."]],[4473,["All money, all earnings are going to the","people. Just to have cheap popularity."]],[4481,["Once all the money is wasted and frittered","away like this, what will happen?"]],[4485,["Even if they have more money, what","will they do? They will just drink."]],[4494,["People are just buying things because they are getting","loans and loans. Everybody is getting a loan there."]],[4499,["They are very anxious to give loans. And","because of that, the pound has gone up."]],[4505,["It is a very artificial way."]],[4508,["The same thing was done with Reagan."]],[4509,["Also, I must say that, in that country they","gave a lot of loans to other countries"]],[4514,["and that’s how they kept up","themselves. But now where are they?"]],[4516,["They cannot raise their","dollar whatever they may try."]],[4524,["I mean, that’s not… that’s a capitalist country","now, as far as that thing is concerned."]],[4530,["They are capitalists who are","ruling. And this is not capitalism."]],[4533,["This is not conservatism. They","are not conserving at all."]],[4546,["And this country is another mess I see."]],[4549,["The labour laws are so high up."]],[4552,["I remember a long time back, my husband used to say that,","“The worst is the labour of Australia.” I said, \"Why?\""]],[4558,["“You see, now they are asking wages for bending."]],[4562,["So now the wages in the whole of our shipping will","go up and we will have problems,” and this and that."]],[4567,["So now they raised the wages of the","labour. Alright. So now what’s happening?"]],[4572,["Because the labour is so expensive,","you cannot produce anything."]],[4576,["Because you cannot produce anything,","so you get everything from abroad."]],[4580,["People are just having their doles:"]],[4582,["no wages, nothing, not working and spending more","for the things they are getting from abroad."]],[4588,["Everything is imported in this","country."]],[4592,["Everything, I was shocked. Everything","is imported in this country."]],[4597,["It’s going to be like Canada,","which is depending on America."]],[4603,["The same thing is even happening in","the television industry, Mother."]],[4606,["One of our problems here in Melbourne,","trying to get television on"]],[4612,["particularly television to take","much interest in Your visit"]],[4616,["is they say, “Oh well, all our programs come from Sydney.”"]],[4619,["So everything’s being imported…"]],[4621,["They are what?"]],[4622,["They all come from Sydney."]],[4624,["All the programs are in Sydney and they","send them down the line to Melbourne."]],[4628,["It’s the same sort of thing is happening within","Australia. Everything is getting smaller and smaller."]],[4634,["Not localised."]],[4635,["No."]],[4636,["But one thing is there. You may","not have localised, ah, this thing."]],[4642,["But supposing tomorrow you start getting","everything from England, then what will happen?"]],[4648,["Everybody will have doles sitting at","home seeing the English programmes."]],[4652,["And then it might only be from","India you might be getting."]],[4657,["After sometime and importing even that."]],[4664,["See, we must not keep our children without any work."]],[4670,["That’s a very dangerous thing."]],[4673,["That’s a very dangerous thing to do."]],[4675,["Oh, I have to take that, I am sorry."]],[4680,["(Hindi) Please get that to eat, what was","brought here just now. Yes, bran, bran."]],[4685,["I will have to, according  to treatment of Mister…"]],[4689,["I’ll  just take a second to have this. Let Me have","that. This is Mister… yes, I will take that."]],[4695,["Yes, what is it?"]],[4698,["Um... I wasn’t going to mention it before the programme Shri Mataji, but there are some negative ex-Sahaja Yogis in Adelaide…"]]]);
